    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG are proud to present 20 Mount Drummond Avenue, Harold's Cross to the market, an attractive and deceptively spacious three-bedroom home which has been thoughtfully upgraded and architecturally designed to create a bright, contemporary and highly versatile family home. The property has been significantly enhanced by an impressive architecturally designed extension to the rear and further benefits from off-street parking to the front and a highly desirable south-facing rear garden.\n\nThe accommodation is particularly impressive at ground-floor level. To the front, the original reception room is currently arranged as a third bedroom, measuring approximately 2.98m x 3.26m. This is an extremely flexible space which could equally function as a separate family room, home office or playroom depending on the requirements of the new owner.\n\nMoving through the property, the spacious kitchen forms the heart of the home and has been fitted with a comprehensive range of contemporary units providing excellent storage and generous worktop space. A breakfast bar provides an informal dining area and creates a natural connection between the kitchen and the extended living accommodation beyond.\n\nThe architecturally designed rear extension is undoubtedly one of the standout features of the property. Designed with an emphasis on space and natural light, it creates an impressive open-plan living and dining area, with two large rooflights flooding the room with daylight. The generous proportions provide ample space for both dining and relaxed family living, while extensive glazing and direct access to the south-facing rear garden create an excellent connection between the indoor and outdoor spaces.\n\nThe result is a home that combines the character and proportions of the original property with a bright, modern extension ideally suited to contemporary family life. Together with its three-bedroom layout, off-street parking and south-facing garden, No. 20 offers an excellent opportunity to acquire a thoughtfully designed home in the heart of Harold's Cross.\n\nThe city centre is within easy walking distance, with numerous bus routes servicing the area. Every conceivable amenity is close by, including a wide selection of shops, pubs, and restaurants, making a car more of a luxury than a necessity. There is also quick and easy pedestrian access to Rathmines, while the vibrant atmosphere of Grafton Street is just a 10-minute walk away. This home offers a perfect oasis on the edge of all the hustle and bustle."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nKitchen - 4.85m x 3.50m\n\n\nDining Area - 2.63m 2.01m\n\n\nLiving Area - 4.85m x 4.01m\n\n\nBedroom - 2.98m x 3.26m\n\n\nBedroom - 3.93m x 3.77m\n\n\nFamily Bathroom - 1.82m x 1.87m\n\n\nBedroom - 2.93m x 2.84m\n\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Architecturally designed and extended three-bedroom home</li><li> Impressive open-plan living and dining extension</li><li> Contemporary fitted kitchen with excellent storage and breakfast bar</li><li> Two large rooflights providing an abundance of natural light</li><li> Highly desirable south-facing rear garden</li><li> Off-street parking to the front</li><li> Flexible ground-floor third bedroom, suitable as a family room or home office</li><li> Generously proportioned principal bedroom</li><li> Guest WC at ground-floor level</li><li> Excellent balance of living and bedroom accommodation</li><li> Bright, modern interiors throughout</li><li> Convenient location in the heart of Harold's Cross</ul>"
